      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "In addition to the existing diagnostic accuracy studies [16-20, 25], our main objective, as a new insight to this field, was to investigate how PoCUS improves clinical endpoints in patients with acute onset dyspnea.",
      "reason": "The review objective is explicitly stated (“main objective… was to investigate how PoCUS improves clinical endpoints…”), but it is not clearly expressed in a relevant question-formulation framework (e.g., explicitly structured question)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "The selected studies had to match our previously defined PICO (Patients, Intervention, Control, Outcome) framework: ... P: Adults and children ... eligible. ... I: The examined intervention was PoCUS use on its own or in combination with conventional diagnostic measures. ... C: Control group included conventional diagnostic methods, such as taking the patients' medical history, physical examination, ECG, blood gas and different laboratory analyses, echocardiography, CXR, or computer tomography (CT).",
      "reason": "Planned comparisons are stated using an explicit PICO framework, including the intervention (PoCUS) and control (conventional diagnostic methods), for eligible patients."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 78
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "The selected studies had to match our previously defined PICO (Patients, Intervention, Control, Outcome) framework: ... P: Adults and children who were admitted to the ED or to the Intensive Care Unit (ICU), or to another inpatient setting because of acute onset or worsening dyspnea were eligible. ... Studies reporting on trauma-induced acute onset dyspnea, or pregnancy were excluded. ... I: The examined intervention was PoCUS use on its own or in combination with conventional diagnostic measures. ... There were no restrictions on the type of PoCUS protocols. ... C: Control group included conventional diagnostic methods, such as taking the patients' medical history, physical examination, ECG, blood gas and different laboratory analyses, echocardiography, CXR, or computer tomography (CT).",
      "reason": "Eligibility is described using the PICO framework, including participants, intervention, and control, and some exclusions are stated. However, the evidence does not specify all study-characteristic components required (e.g., eligible study designs/settings are partially described, and follow-up requirements are not reported here)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "We did not use any restrictions or limitations based on language or publication date.",
      "reason": "The review reports no language restrictions and no publication-date restrictions. However, it does not explicitly state eligibility criteria for report characteristics such as dissemination year and publication/report status (e.g., unpublished/ongoing/grey literature)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No evidence is provided that the review distinguishes exclusion due to outcomes not measured versus outcomes not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The evidence does not describe which groups were used in each synthesis or how those groups map to the comparisons in the review objectives."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "Although inclusion/exclusion criteria are listed, the evidence does not provide rationales for notable restrictions on eligibility."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 62
}

